.TH ZERODDS-GRPC-BRIDGED 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-grpc-bridged \- DDS to gRPC bridge daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-grpc-bridged
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-bind\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-\-domain\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-reflection\fR]
[\fB\-\-topic\fR \fIDDS:SVC\fR]...
[\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-grpc-bridged
exposes each mapped DDS topic as a gRPC service:
.B Publish
writes the
.I Sample
payload to the topic,
.B Subscribe
returns the next sample (one per call). The payload is opaque bytes, the
DDS user data as it is. TLS with ALPN
.IR h2 ,
mTLS, bearer and JWT authentication, a topic ACL and the reflection
service are served; the
.I grpc-timeout
header is not applied. Implements
.IR docs/specs/zerodds-grpc-bridge-1.0.md .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config =\fIFILE\fR
YAML config (Spec \(sc3). See
.BR zerodds-grpc-bridged.yaml (5).
.TP
.BR \-\-bind =\fIADDR\fR
HTTP/2 bind addr. Default:
.IR 0.0.0.0:50051 .
Without TLS only a loopback address (127.0.0.0/8, ::1, localhost) starts
(cleartext h2c, Spec \(sc4.1); another one is exit 1.
.TP
.BR \-\-domain =\fIID\fR
DDS Domain ID. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-cert =\fIFILE\fR
TLS cert PEM.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-key =\fIFILE\fR
TLS key PEM.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-client\-ca =\fIFILE\fR
CA PEM for client certificates (mTLS).
.TP
.BR \-\-reflection
Enable the gRPC reflection service.
.TP
.BR \-\-topic =\fIDDS:SVC\fR
Inline topic mapping override.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level =\fILEVEL\fR
One of
.IR trace ", " debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error :
the threshold of the JSON log on stdout. Every call that ended is one line
with
.B \(dqevent\(dq:\(dqrpc\(dq
and peer, service, method, dds_topic, bytes, grpc_status, latency_us and
stream_id, at info when it ended OK and at warn otherwise.
.TP
.BR \-\-metrics =\fIADDR\fR
Prometheus listen addr.
.PP
Test hooks. Real options, documented because the program accepts them
and an option nobody can find is one nobody maintains.
.TP
.BR \-\-once
Serve one request, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-idle\-timeout\-ms =\fIN\fR
Exit after \fIN\fR milliseconds without a request.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the option synopsis.
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable;
.BI + PATH = VALUE
appends to a list.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate and print the effective configuration with the origin of every
value, then exit: 0 valid, 1 invalid value or unknown key (also an auth
mode that cannot be served and tenants without TLS and a client CA, as at
the start), 2 unreadable file, syntax error or include cycle. The TLS
material is loaded at the start only.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGTERM and SIGINT start the drain: the listening socket closes, every
connection gets GOAWAY(NO_ERROR) with the last stream the client opened, the
calls up to it run on, a new stream is refused with
RST_STREAM(REFUSED_STREAM). Calls still open after
.B grpc.drain_secs
(default 30) end with UNAVAILABLE. Within the same time the daemon waits for
the acknowledgements of its DDS writes, then deletes its DDS entities and
exits 0.
SIGHUP reads the configuration again: the TLS certificate and key, the
auth settings and the topic ACL apply from then on (the certificate to new
connections). Changed binds, domain, topic mappings, reflection or TLS on
or off need a restart and are logged; the auth settings are checked against
the bind that is served, so
.B auth.mode: none
in a file that also moves the bind to loopback is refused on a daemon bound
to another address. A configuration that does not load, or that cannot be
served, changes nothing.
.SH WINDOWS SERVICE
Started by the service control manager, the daemon runs as the service
.BR ZeroDDSGrpcBridge :
start pending until it serves, then running; the stop and shutdown
controls are SIGTERM (stop pending, the drain),
.B sc.exe control ZeroDDSGrpcBridge paramchange
is SIGHUP; when it ends, the service is stopped with the exit status below.
Started from a console, Ctrl+C, Ctrl+Break and the closing of the console
are SIGTERM.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
Optional OTLP endpoint http://\fIhost\fR[:\fIport\fR],
such as http://localhost:4318 (port 80 when it is missing): the daemon
sends a server span per call
.RI ( service / method ,
with a dds.publish or dds.subscribe child) as OTLP/HTTP JSON to its
/v1/traces, every 5 s and at the stop. The exporter speaks no TLS and
posts at the root: https, a path, a query or a port that is not a number
stops the start with exit status 1. A failed export loses its spans and
logs
.B otlp_export_failed
at warn, at most once a minute. A call with a W3C
.B traceparent
header continues the caller's trace; one whose caller did not sample it
records nothing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 normal stop, 1 configuration (also an auth mode that cannot be served,
such as
.B jwt
without
.BR auth.jwt.public_key ,
or an
.B OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
the exporter cannot serve),
2 bind (port in use), 3 a DDS participant that does not start (also a
tenant's), 4 TLS material that does not load.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/zerodds/grpc-bridged.yaml .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-grpc-bridged.yaml (5),
.BR grpcurl (1).
